  "details": "We all know the purpose of both cameras. But why can't I have two cameras out? What would it break having it out? \n\nThe idea leans more towards content creators (streamers). What if I wanna take a quick photo? Answer: You can snap a photo with the stream camera too! \n\nWhile that is true, what it also does is forces us to move our setup. I like to try and keep my stream camera in one spot and as stationary as possible. I know you can also setup presets too but that's annoying in and of itself. Not to mention what if we want to use the print camera.. it disables the \"stream camera\" mode so if you are streaming/recording, you are forced back into FPP/POV cam. Photo/Print camera's should just be the same camera with a mode swap while stream camera needs it's own asset/function\n\nSpawning in a separate camera for pictures only would be nice. Swapping modes is cool but having the option for this would be cool too\n\nHow many people would use this if was a feature? I don't know, most people don't even know how to use any of the cameras let alone how they function. I see it all the time with new users and even OGs..",
